{"kind":"artifact","text":"Replacement docs artifact for the documentation re-anchor at exact head ee42fe052a527d402e795c35204928520a5df0a8, superseding my earlier 703074f5, which was stale from birth.\n\nThe head is unchanged. It repoints twelve documentation pages from four superseded spike-path artifacts to their live same-path successors, so the predecessors can be retired without a retired citation reddening the docset gate, and it corrects one piece of prose in docs/reference/gs/actors.md: a retired membership does not remove a principal from the roster, it leaves the row standing with retired true and an empty roles list, so a reader is told to read the flag rather than the absence, and that custody and retired can disagree.\n\nWhy the earlier artifact was stale from birth, and what changed here. It was directed to rest on the two spike-path artifacts the pages now cite, 265b1472 at spike/internal/workroom and c20ea289 at spike, and both of those were already stale, so the docs artifact inherited their staleness the moment it was signed and no merge could accept it. The correction is in the bases, not the tree. This artifact rests on two behaviour pointers that are live and non-stale: b78567c9 at path spike for commit 8f0b86f3, freshly published, and the existing 3514c481 at path internal/workroom for the same commit. Those are the paths the twelve pages actually describe, since the workroom package moved to the repository root in 8b112bb7 and spike/internal/workroom has held nothing since. Nothing is published at that deleted path.\n\nVerified at this head, no file changed. ee42fe05 is still the tip of request/docs-spike-predecessor-reanchor. Its merge base with main is exactly 8f0b86f3; main has since moved twelve commits to f8ce4892 and none of them touch any of the twelve pages; the branch merges clean. The actors.md correction matches the shipped code at internal/app/app.go:1279, where ActorViews passes Retired and Custody straight through, at internal/a